workedExamples.solution_text:
Split the integral where the formula changes.
$\begin{align*}\int_{-3}^0 k(3+x)\,dx+\int_0^3 k(3-x)\,dx&=1\\k\left[3x+\frac{x^2}{2}\right]_{-3}^0+k\left[3x-\frac{x^2}{2}\right]_0^3&=1\\\frac{9k}{2}+\frac{9k}{2}&=1\\9k&=1\\k&=\frac{1}{9}\end{align*}$
The sketch shows the two pieces meeting at height $3k=\frac{1}{3}$. Both pieces are nonnegative.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=60mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (-3.7,0)--(3.8,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,-0.05)--(0,0.43);
\draw[black,thick] (-3,0)--(0,{1/3})--(3,0);
\draw[black] (-3,0.008)--(-3,-0.008) (3,0.008)--(3,-0.008);
\path (-3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-3$} (3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$} (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\path (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,0.43) node[above] {$f(x)$} (0,{1/3}) node[above left] {$\frac{1}{3}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The function $f(x) = ax^{2}$ on $[0,2]$, and $0$ elsewhere, is a probability density function.
Find $a$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.8cm, y=1.2cm]
\fill[gray!35, domain=0:2, variable=\x] (0,0) -- plot ({\x},{3*\x*\x/8}) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0) -- (3.0,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.1) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.3,0) -- (0,0);
\draw[thick, domain=0:2, smooth, samples=100, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*\x*\x/8});
\draw[thick] (2,0) -- (2.8,0);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

